<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    TUnitAnalyzerCanary — the non-vacuity fixture for the TUnit analyzer gate
    (#1836). NOT a test suite and NOT a row of Harbor.slnx.

    WHAT IT IS
    A project whose only content is two planted TUnitAssertions0005 offences:
    one that must be reported and one that is waived and must NOT be. The
    gate tool (tools/check-tunit-analyzer-gate.py) builds this project and
    asserts exactly that outcome, so the gate is proved rather than assumed.

    WHY IT IS NOT IN THE SOLUTION
    Because the planted offender is an ERROR: tests/Directory.Build.props
    promotes TUnitAssertions0005 to an error, so a project carrying one
    cannot be part of a build that has to stay green. Keeping it out of
    Harbor.slnx is what lets the canary exist at all — and it is why the
    canary is built by exactly one job, which expects the failure.

    WHY IT LIVES UNDER tests/
    Because the policy under test is the one in tests/Directory.Build.props
    (the promotion of TUnitAssertions0005 to an error). A canary outside
    tests/ would inherit the root props instead, where TreatWarningsAsErrors
    is true for every diagnostic — and then it would prove nothing about the
    promotion this change adds.

    IsTestProject is false on purpose: nothing here is a test to RUN, and the
    flag decides whether Directory.Build.targets hands the project a TUnit
    reference. The reference is declared explicitly below instead, so this
    file says what it needs rather than relying on a convention.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <IsTestProject>false</IsTestProject>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      The TUnit package is what carries the analyzer assemblies
      (TUnit.Analyzers inside TUnit.Core, TUnit.Assertions.Analyzers inside
      TUnit.Assertions). Without this reference the canary would compile with
      no analyzer at all and would prove nothing — which is exactly the
      failure this fixture exists to catch.
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="TUnit"/>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
